  "summary": "TOK1 is AirTrunk's flagship hyperscale campus in the Inzai data center hub east of Tokyo, which AirTrunk bills as the biggest hyperscale campus in Japan measured in megawatts. The 13-hectare campus is scalable to more than 300 MW and already has facilities in service. In August 2024 AirTrunk said a 50 MW third phase was on schedule and topping out; it broke ground on a further 40 MW-plus phase in June 2025, and in March 2026 said it had recently begun building over 100 MW of additional IT load. That month it closed a JPY 191.6 billion green loan to refinance existing TOK1 facilities and fund the next phases.",
